The upstream project provides the GGUF reader integration, the GGML custom
operations, the dequantisation kernels and all non-qwen35 model support.

Changes made in this fork (2026, IKBlue):

  * qwen35_support.py (new file)
      Remaps a raw Qwen3.5 ("qwen35") GGUF text encoder onto ComfyUI's native
      qwen35 checkpoint layout: key renaming, the RMSNorm +1 centring offset,
      the ssm_a -> A_log log transform, the value-head channel permutation and
      the conv1d channel-group order.  Tensors are dequantised on return so
      that load_state_dict sees real storage shapes.
      Also provides vision_from_mmproj(), which converts a Qwen3.5 mmproj GGUF
      (llama.cpp vision tower) into ComfyUI's model.visual.* layout, for text
      encoder GGUFs that were exported language-only.

  * loader.py (modified)
      "qwen35" added to TXT_ARCH_LIST; an early qwen35 branch added to
      gguf_clip_loader() delegating to qwen35_support, with an optional
      vision_path argument that merges the mmproj vision tower.

  * nodes.py (modified)
      CLIPLoaderGGUF gains an optional "vision_name" widget so a matching
      mmproj GGUF can be selected alongside the text encoder.

No other files were modified.  See README.md for verification details.
